{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1157 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "05839a62dc31c1231203698f9f850076117b11824d395270eec25a47823d03f7" :edb/db-before-t 1156 :edb/db-after-t 1157 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534469 50 #inst "2026-10-11T21:49:54.795Z" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186198842 1071 "Describe the set $S=\\{5,6,7,...,50\\}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}\\}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186198842 1071 "Describe the set $S={5,6,7,...,50}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS={x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false] [17592186198842 1074 "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers between $5$ and $50$ (including $5$ and $50$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in N\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50\\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50\\}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $4<x<51.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in N\\,:\\,4<x<51\\},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,4<x<51\\}.\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186198842 1074 "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers between $5$ and $50$ (including $5$ and $50$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $4<x<51.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,4<x<51},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,4<x<51}.\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false] [17592186198844 1071 "Describe the set $S=\\{…,3,6,12,24,48,...\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=6$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\nS=\\{{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}}\\}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186198844 1071 "Describe the set $S={…,3,6,12,24,48,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=6$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\nS={{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}}}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false] [17592186198844 1074 "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,3,\\,6,\\,12,\\,24,\\,48,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{12} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=6,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS=\\{3\\cdot {2}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in Z\\}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186198844 1074 "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,3,\\,6,\\,12,\\,24,\\,48,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{12} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=6,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={3\\cdot {2}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false] [17592186287857 1071 "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set $\\{-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}\\}$ given below.\n\n$\\{-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}\\}=\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0\\}$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186287857 1071 "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}$ given below.\n\n${-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0}$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false] [17592186287857 1074 "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some cubic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=-\\sqrt{5},$ and ${x}_{3}=\\sqrt{5},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(3)(x-(-3))(x-(-\\sqrt{5}))(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x+\\sqrt{5})(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-\\sqrt{5}x+\\sqrt{5}x-(\\sqrt{5})^{2}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-5) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5x+3{x}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as\n\n$$\n\\{-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}\\}=\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45=0\\}.\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186287857 1074 "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some cubic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=-\\sqrt{5},$ and ${x}_{3}=\\sqrt{5},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(3)(x-(-3))(x-(-\\sqrt{5}))(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x+\\sqrt{5})(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-\\sqrt{5}x+\\sqrt{5}x-(\\sqrt{5})^{2}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-5) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5x+3{x}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as\n\n$$\n{-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45=0}.\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false] [17592186396254 1071 "Describe the set $S=\\{-6,-5,-4,...,12\\}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}\\}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186396254 1071 "Describe the set $S={-6,-5,-4,...,12}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS={x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false] [17592186396254 1074 "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-6$ and $12$ (including $-6$ and $12$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,-6\\le x\\le 12\\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $-7<x<13.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,-7<x<13\\}.\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186396254 1074 "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-6$ and $12$ (including $-6$ and $12$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,-6\\le x\\le 12}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $-7<x<13.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,-7<x<13}.\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false] [17592186412792 1071 "Describe the set $S=\\{…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x<{{field-2}}\\}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186412792 1071 "Describe the set $S={…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS={x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x<{{field-2}}}\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false] [17592186412792 1074 "The set $S$ contains all integers less than $3,$ including $3.$\n\nIn other words, $S$ contains all integers less than $4,$  *excluding* $4.$ \n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,x<4\\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\le 3.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,x\\le 3\\}.\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 true] [17592186412792 1074 "The set $S$ contains all integers less than $3,$ including $3.$\n\nIn other words, $S$ contains all integers less than $4,$  *excluding* $4.$ \n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x<4}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\le 3.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x\\le 3}.\n$$" 13194139534469 17592186045417 false]] :edb/tempids {}}
